      "The third law states that when object A exerts a force on object B, B exerts a force of equal size and opposite direction on A. The two forces of the pair act on different objects, so they never cancel each other. A rocket pushes exhaust gas backward and the gas pushes the rocket forward; a swimmer pushes water back and the water pushes the swimmer ahead."
